    "representation": "All recognized runes in archived order, including headings. Ignore other characters. Empty pages contribute no candidates.",
    "procedure": "Apply Fibonacci shifts F_0=0, F_1=1, F_(n+2)=F_(n+1)+F_n modulo 29, with both subtraction and addition. Compare the first 12 output indices with nine fixed known openings; retain full candidates.",
    "parameters": "Offsets 0–28 inclusive; two directions; independent page reset; one term per rune; no interruptions. 55 rune-bearing pages, 3190 candidates, 28710 comparisons.",
    "exclusions": "Other beginnings, offsets above 28, interruptions, heading removal, reversed input, word or row resets, cross-page carry, other numerical schedules and language scoring."
  },
  "outcome": "not-supported",
  "finding": "Zero fixed-opening matches among 1540 distinct page outputs. All 3190 nominal configurations reproduce. The independent checker verifies the exact 14-term residue cycle and every repeated-offset equivalence.",
  "limitations": "Only nine fixed 12-rune beginnings; no general language score or interruptions. Repeated configurations are not extra coverage or independent evidence. The experiment does not establish Fibonacci numbers as an intended manuscript key. Computational review only; human review pending.",
  "next_steps": "Do not extend the starting-offset range under unchanged rules: all 14 phases are covered. Declare different seeds, interruptions, boundary rules or plaintext criteria separately.",
